{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"fraction operations fraction operations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md","fileName":"Fraction Operations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Fraction Operations","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Fractions and Decimal Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Common Denominator","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"fraction operations fraction operations","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md","fileName":"Fraction Operations.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Fraction Operations","heading":"Fraction Operations","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Fraction operations preserve the meanings of addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division while expressing results as quotients. Addition and subtraction first use a [[Common Denominator]]:\n\n$$\\frac{a}{b}+\\frac{c}{d}=\\frac{ad+bc}{bd},\\qquad\n\\frac{a}{b}-\\frac{c}{d}=\\frac{ad-bc}{bd}.$$\n\nMultiplication combines corresponding components, ((a/b)(c/d)=ac/bd). Division by a nonzero fraction multiplies by its [[Reciprocal]], ((a/b)\\div(c/d)=ad/bc). Common factors may be cancelled before or after an operation to simplify the result.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Fractions and Decimal Forms","Common Denominator","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Fraction Operations.md"